{"signature": "{\"text\": \"Here is a GCSE-style question. A cyclist and bicycle have a combined mass of 80 kilograms and travel at six metres per second. Part A, worth three marks: calculate their kinetic energy. Part B, worth two marks: explain what happens to their kinetic energy if their speed doubles. For Part A, one half multiplied by 80 multiplied by six squared equals 40 multiplied by 36, giving 1,440 joules. Award one mark for the equation or correct use of the squared speed, one for substitution and one for the answer with its unit. For Part B, kinetic energy is proportional to speed squared. Doubling speed gives two squared, which is four, so the kinetic energy becomes four times as large. Award one mark for the squared relationship and one for the factor of four.\", \"voice\": \"en-NG-AbeoNeural\", \"rate\": \"-4%\", \"eleven\": false}", "duration": 52.68, "words": [["Here", 0.102083], ["is", 0.3495], ["a", 0.466666], ["GCSE-style", 0.583875], ["question.", 1.44325], ["A", 2.838541], ["cyclist", 2.96875], ["and", 3.489583], ["bicycle", 3.697916], ["have", 4.114583], ["a", 4.296875], ["combined", 4.414083], ["mass", 4.869791], ["of", 5.078125], ["80", 5.221375], ["kilograms", 5.533875], ["and", 6.184916], ["travel", 6.354166], ["at", 6.70575], ["six", 6.875], ["metres", 7.161458], ["per", 7.578125], ["second.", 7.695333], ["Part", 9.127625], ["A,", 9.401041], ["worth", 9.882833], ["three", 10.208333], ["marks:", 10.403666], ["calculate", 11.09375], ["their", 11.5625], ["kinetic", 11.757833], ["energy.", 12.239583], ["Part", 13.645833], ["B,", 13.958333], ["worth", 14.453125], ["two", 14.778666], ["marks:", 14.934916], ["explain", 15.533875], ["what", 15.976583], ["happens", 16.145833], ["to", 16.510416], ["their", 16.653666], ["kinetic", 16.835958], ["energy", 17.317708], ["if", 17.7995], ["their", 17.96875], ["speed", 18.151041], ["doubles.", 18.4375], ["For", 19.921875], ["Part", 20.260416], ["A,", 20.494791], ["one", 20.989583], ["half", 21.223958], ["